Okay, well, often it is easiest to write what something isn't rather than what it is. So what is sustainability not?

It is not a silver bullet, it probably isn't the "easiest" way.

±±±

Sustainability is complex, but it is also simple. It is a conundrum? The systems, ramifications, technical specifics, etc. of sustainability may be complex, but the over arching philosophy is simple.

±±±

Nature was first. We cannot exist outside of nature. Therefore, our society is a sub-set of nature. We created the "economy" so likewise, that does not exist outside of our society. Thus economy is a subset of society.

nature » society » economy.

With this view it is impossible to see the economy as more important than society or nature — it would not exist without them, without us.

±±±

Sustainability is more than an adjective. It is a way of thinking. A philosophy.
